-- title:
--   Descent from a real cone to a rational cone
-- statement:
--   Let $I$ be finite, $J$ any index type, $A_i,b\in\mathbb Q^J$, and $x_i\in\mathbb R$ with $x_i\ge0$. If $\sum_i x_i A_{i,j}=b_j$ for every coordinate $j$, then
--   \[
--   b\in\operatorname{cone}_{\mathbb Q}\{A_i:i\in I\}.
--   \]
--   The cone consists of finite nonnegative rational linear combinations. This turns real nonnegative solutions of rational systems into rational conic certificates.
